cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Warrant: signed, hash-addressed decision records for AI agents"
abstract: >-
  A record format for agent decisions. Each record states what was decided, under
  which policy pinned by the hash of its exact bytes, because of which reasons,
  on which evidence — signed by the actor and addressed by its own hash. Reasons
  may be deterministic bounded computations that any reader re-executes offline,
  so a decision's justification can be checked without trusting whoever produced
  the log. Includes settlement semantics, key-state with threshold governance,
  and three implementations that agree byte-exact on every conformance vector.
message: "If you use or evaluate this work, please cite it."
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/s0fractal/warrant"
